# Bug Fix Summary for Shell Project

## Overview
Three bugs were identified in Parts 1-5 that need fixing before implementing Part 6.

## Detailed Changes

### Issue #18: EOF Handling
**File:** lexer.c
```c
// Line 24, after the while loop
if (buffer == NULL) {
    return NULL;  // EOF encountered
}
```

**File:** main.c  
```c
// Line 32, after get_input()
if (input == NULL) {
    printf("\n");  // Print newline for clean exit
    break;  // Exit the shell on EOF
}
```

### Issue #19: PATH Search Bug
**File:** main.c
```c
// Lines 76-112: Restructured logic
if (strchr(first_token, '/') != NULL) {
    // Direct execution for paths with slashes
    exec_path = malloc(strlen(first_token) + 1);
    strcpy(exec_path, first_token);
} else {
    // PATH search only for commands without slashes
    // ... existing PATH search code ...
}
```

### Issue #20: Hostname Fallback
**File:** main.c
```c
// Lines 14-23: Add fallback for MACHINE
char *machine = getenv("MACHINE");
char hostname[256];
if (!machine) {
    if (gethostname(hostname, sizeof(hostname)) == 0) {
        machine = hostname;
    } else {
        machine = "localhost";
    }
}
```

## Testing Verification

### Before Fixes
```bash
# Issue #18: Hangs
echo "ls" | ./bin/shell  # Infinite loop

# Issue #19: Fails
./test_script.sh         # Command not found
/bin/ls                  # Command not found

# Issue #20: Shows null
unset MACHINE && ./bin/shell  # user@(null):path>
```

### After Fixes
```bash
# Issue #18: Clean exit
echo "ls" | ./bin/shell  # Lists files, exits

# Issue #19: Works
./test_script.sh         # Executes directly
/bin/ls                  # Executes directly

# Issue #20: Shows hostname
unset MACHINE && ./bin/shell  # user@hostname:path>
```
